<title>FINLAND: PELLERVO SEES 2.5 PCT FINNISH 1997 GDP GROWTH.</title>
<headline>PELLERVO SEES 2.5 PCT FINNISH 1997 GDP GROWTH.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pellervo Institute of</p>
<p>Economic Research (PTT) said in a new forecast on Thursday that</p>
<p>a recession in continental Europe would slow the Finnish</p>
<p>economic recovery.</p>
<p>PTT forecast Finnish economic growth at 2.5 percent in 1997,</p>
<p>up from two percent growth projected for this year.</p>
<p>The institute's GDP forecasts were unchanged compared to its</p>
<p>previous forecast released in April.</p>
<p>Key figures in PTT's 1996/2 forecast:</p>
<p>				 1996	1997	1995</p>
<p> GDP			     +2	+2.5	+4.2</p>
<p> Imports			 +1	  +6	+6.3</p>
<p> Exports			 +1	  +5	+8.3</p>
<p> Consumption		 +2.5	+2.5	+3.1</p>
<p>   private		     +3	  +3	+3.8</p>
<p>   public		    +1.5	  +1	+1.3</p>
<p> Investment		  +3.5	  +3	+7.7</p>
<p>   private		     +3	  +2     +10.9</p>
<p>   public			+5	  +8	-6.1</p>
<p> CPI			   +0.5	+1.0	+1.0</p>
<p> Unemployment (pct)	16.6	16.1	17.2</p>
<p> C/A (bln markka)	   +20	 +20     +24.5</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
